---
import UniPage from '../components/UniPage.astro';
import { getUniversity } from '../data/universities';

const uni = getUniversity('ktu')!;
---

<UniPage
  uni={uni}
  title="KTU CGPA to Percentage Calculator (Unified CGPA × 10 Formula) | GlobalCGPA"
  description="Convert KTU CGPA to percentage using the unified CGPA × 10 formula (U.O. 3078/2023). Replaces older scheme-specific formulas. Free calculator with reverse conversion, conversion table, class thresholds and FAQ."
  intro="Enter your KTU CGPA to get your percentage using the current unified CGPA × 10 formula — plus reverse conversion, a reference table and KTU class thresholds for placements and higher studies."
>
  <h2>How the KTU CGPA to Percentage Conversion Works</h2>
  <p>APJ Abdul Kalam Technological University (KTU) now uses a single unified formula for all UG and PG programmes across all schemes, per <strong>U.O. No. 3078/2023/KTU (26 Nov 2023)</strong>:</p>
  <div class="formula-block">
    <div class="f-label">KTU current formula (all schemes)</div>
    <div class="f-text">Percentage = CGPA × 10</div>
  </div>
  <p>Under the current rule, an 8.5 CGPA is exactly 85% and a perfect 10.0 is 100%. This unified formula replaced earlier scheme-specific offset formulas through a series of university orders in 2023.</p>

  <h3>Worked Examples (Current Formula)</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>CGPA</th><th>Current Formula (×10)</th><th>Old B.Tech 2019 (10×CGPA−2.5)</th><th>Old M.Tech 2015 (10×CGPA−3.75)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>9.0</td><td>90%</td><td>87.5%</td><td>86.25%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>8.5</td><td>85%</td><td>82.5%</td><td>81.25%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>8.0</td><td>80%</td><td>77.5%</td><td>76.25%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>7.0</td><td>70%</td><td>67.5%</td><td>66.25%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>6.5</td><td>65%</td><td>62.5%</td><td>61.25%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Historical Context: The 2023 Revisions</h2>
  <p>KTU unified its conversion through three university orders in 2023:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>U.O. No. 1584/2023/KTU (29 Jun 2023):</strong> Changed B.Tech 2019 scheme from <code>Percentage = (10 × CGPA) − 2.5</code> to <code>CGPA × 10</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>U.O. No. 1867/2023/KTU (27 Jul 2023):</strong> Extended the <code>CGPA × 10</code> formula to the B.Tech 2015 scheme.</li>
    <li><strong>U.O. No. 3078/2023/KTU (26 Nov 2023):</strong> Unified all UG and PG programmes across all schemes under <code>Percentage = CGPA × 10</code>, including M.Tech 2015 (which previously used <code>(10 × CGPA) − 3.75</code>).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Certificates issued before the respective amendments retain their original converted percentages. For current conversions and new certificates, use <code>CGPA × 10</code>.</p>

  <h2>KTU Class Thresholds</h2>
  <p>KTU awards <strong>First Class with Honours</strong> at roughly 8.5 CGPA and above, <strong>First Class</strong> from about 6.5 CGPA (65% under the current formula), and <strong>Second Class</strong> below that, with the degree itself requiring a minimum CGPA around 5.0. Honours awards can carry additional conditions in your specific scheme, such as completing extra credits or clearing all subjects within the standard duration, so check your regulation if you are near the 8.5 boundary.</p>
  <p>For placements, the practical cut-offs are simple: most service-based companies filter at 6.0–6.5 CGPA (60–65%) and competitive product roles at 7.5+ (75%). KTU's CGPA is a credit-weighted average of your semester SGPAs — if you want to project it before consolidation, use our <a href="/sgpa-to-cgpa">SGPA to CGPA calculator</a>, which applies the same credit-weighting KTU does.</p>

  <h2>Using Your KTU Percentage</h2>
  <p>Within India — for Kerala PSC applications, GATE counselling, campus placements and scholarships — the ×10 percentage from this calculator is the figure to quote alongside your CGPA. For foreign universities, submit your original CGPA with the scale noted (for example, "8.2/10.0, KTU India") and let credential evaluators handle the conversion; our <a href="/cgpa-to-gpa">CGPA to GPA converter</a> gives you a quick linear estimate for self-assessment.</p>
</UniPage>
